- 2026-10-30 22:33 UTC: The Pi view is built (73827674, `src/harness/agents/pi-view/`): a worker in Pi on a rig that runs terminals draws Thermite's view of its own Pi session with `@earendil-works/pi-tui` 1.3.0 (MIT, published 2026-10-15, with `marked` 18.0.11 and `get-east-asian-width` 1.6.0; its `native/` is deleted in the harness, supervisor and control images, each build fails if it is left, and the release check refuses it), in the terminal host as the lane's agent user. The owner's input reaches the worker over its trial's routes (`/v1/trial/console/next`, `done`, `end`), one call in the loop per input: words steer, or wait until the agent would stop with the new `follow_up` (core, Live, REST, MCP, `thermite command`); Esc stops the reply once a running tool ends, and the trial goes on without counting it as the agent's stop; `/compact`, `/mcp`, `/mcp reconnect [server]` (the gateway's `?fresh=`) and `/status`; `/skill:NAME` says that the run's kit carries no skills. Each input is recorded with its outcome, and Live shows the view (`pi_view`). The view draws model and tool text with control characters taken out, and pi-tui's images, links and clipboard writes off. Tests pass on the Mac, 66 of 66 in the touched files (pi-view commands, console, view, without its native folder, and the loop; consoles, gateway, compaction, release checks, dashboard); the host's Pi profile test is Linux only. `scripts/acceptance/agents.mjs` gains a Pi scene with each command. Not measured: the view's memory in the image. History's words don't yet say "follow-up" (the event records it, and Live's list shows it).
- 2026-10-30 23:49 UTC: On 73827674 the terminal, rig image and compose smoke acceptance checks pass, and the agents check fails: a worker in Pi could not start its Pi view, because its terminal host, run as the lane's agent user, could not open its socket in the trials' folder, which only the harness could pass through. Every trial ended at once with that error, and the lanes waited ever longer. The Mac's tests run every role as one user, so they could not see it. The trials' folder can now be passed through but not listed (`spawnTrial`); each trial's folder stays its worker's own; the worker's result is made readable on purpose, whatever the umask; and the harness logs a warning when a view can't start or leaves no result. The worker also runs from source under `SOURCE=1`. The terminal check gains a Pi view scene under the real broker as `agent-1`: one short trial to its result with the owner's words, `/status`, a refused command and Esc, and probes that lane-1 and another agent can't list the trials' folder or reach the trial's folder or its socket. Tests: `spawn.test.ts` on the Mac. Next: the terminal and agents acceptance checks on this fix.
- 2026-10-31 00:04 UTC: The Pi view passes its acceptance checks on 5ee8a93b. Terminal: the new Pi view scene runs a worker in Pi as `agent-1` under the real broker to its result; lane-1 and agent-2 each get EACCES listing the trials' folder, entering the trial's folder and reaching its socket; words steer, `/status` shows its counts, `/model` is refused in words, Esc stops the reply; the last screen is kept and nothing of `agent-1`'s is left. Agents: 19 checks pass, among them lane-2's Pi view taking each of the nine inputs (typed, or refused in words), each recorded word for word with its outcome, the model getting the steered words and the follow-up, one compaction, and Live showing the view. With the rig image and compose smoke checks of 73827674, the Pi view's touched checks all pass. Next: the planner and the advisors in their terminals, and the token measurement of Claude Code's terminal against `-p` (gate C, the owner's yes and time).
